  "results": {
    "positive": "Two events accepted at signed limit; valid full-spool events return typed DroppedError with sensor/event/sequence only after C05 publishes markers. Exact retry preserves one marker. Loss query returns count and coalesced sequence ranges after reopen; event after a gap succeeds after signed capacity increase.",
    "negative": "Malformed input never writes a gap; different bytes at the same dropped sequence return storage conflict; global C05 quota failure leaves manifest and loss query unchanged; nil, cancelled and closed queries return explicit errors.",
    "restart": "C05 real file store reopens and rebuilds loss count/ranges from gap records.",
    "discovery": "Four engine suites and 81 required anchors executed and accepted by the discovery guard.",
    "network": "Focused C15 overflow tests passed under strace with zero network syscalls.",
    "workflow": "Local provider, browser, package checksum and clean-clone workflow equivalents passed; no GitHub-hosted run."
  },
  "security_review": [
    "Existing C04 event validation and C11 applied signed settings are checked inside the C05 writer transaction.",
    "Gap markers retain sensor/event identity, sequence and SHA-256 of omitted exact bytes, never the event payload.",
    "C05 operation and disk quotas bound marker growth; quota errors are explicit.",
    "No database schema, network listener/client, UI/CLI surface or dependency added."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Every accepted event remains pending until C16 implements durable ACK and reclamation; markers remain loss history.",
    "C14 readers reject the new gap record type, so rollback after a marker is written requires a C15-compatible reader.",
    "Local clone and injected-error checks are not physical power-loss or GitHub Actions proof; C28 resource capacity is unmeasured.",
    "No standalone JavaScript lint script is defined; formatting, Go vet, TypeScript, tests and builds were run."
  ],
  "rollback": "Keep C05 event bytes and gap history together; never restore an older manifest to erase accepted data or markers.",
